<section class="protocol">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Also on some rather older computers</h2>
    <p class="intro">
      Rachel also runs on the VIC-20 and Commodore 64. Both versions play
      solo with up to seven computer opponents, without a modem or server.
      The VIC-20 needs an 8KB memory expansion; the C64 uses its own RAM.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      The C64 development build can also reconnect to an interrupted online
      game and recover its seat and hand. Solo play and network recovery have
      been tested in emulation. Physical hardware testing is still pending,
      and there is currently no public server for vintage multiplayer.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/ports#c64">See Rachel on the C64</a>,
      <a href="/ports#vic20">explore the VIC-20 release</a>, or
      <a href="/protocol">read the shared network protocol</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

